# React Mobile-First Development with shadcn/ui

## TypeScript Usage Policy

- Do not use `any` (and avoid `unknown` where possible); prefer precise, explicit types.
- Define component props with interfaces/types; extend from `React.ComponentProps<...>` when appropriate.
- Prefer discriminated unions, generics, and utility types over casts; avoid `as` except when narrowing external data.
- Do not use `React.FC`; explicitly type `children?: React.ReactNode` on props when needed.
- All examples should demonstrate proper typing without `any`.

## shadcn/ui Component Usage

### Always Use Existing Components
- Import from `@/components/ui/` - Button, Input, Label, Checkbox, Dialog, Select, Card, etc.
- Follow the established pattern from [resources/js/components/ui/button.tsx](mdc:resources/js/components/ui/button.tsx):
  ```tsx
  import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
  import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input';
  import { Label } from '@/components/ui/label';
  ```

### Adding New Components from shadcn/ui
If a required component doesn't exist in `@/components/ui/`:

1. **Check Documentation**: Visit [shadcn/ui components](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) to see available components
2. **Install Component**: Use the shadcn CLI to add the component:
   ```bash
   npx shadcn@latest add button
   npx shadcn@latest add dialog
   npx shadcn@latest add form
   npx shadcn@latest add select
   npx shadcn@latest add card
   ```
3. **Automatic Setup**: The component will be automatically added to `resources/js/components/ui/`
4. **Configuration**: Component styling is managed through [components.json](mdc:components.json)

#### Available shadcn/ui Components
Common components you can add:
- **Layout**: `card`, `sheet`, `dialog`, `drawer`, `sidebar`
- **Forms**: `form`, `input`, `select`, `checkbox`, `radio-group`, `switch`, `textarea`
- **Navigation**: `tabs`, `breadcrumb`, `pagination`, `navigation-menu`
- **Data Display**: `table`, `badge`, `avatar`, `separator`, `skeleton`
- **Feedback**: `alert`, `toast`, `progress`, `spinner`
- **Overlays**: `popover`, `tooltip`, `dropdown-menu`, `context-menu`
- **Media**: `aspect-ratio`, `image`

#### Example Usage After Installation
```tsx
// After running: npx shadcn@latest add dialog
import { Dialog, DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle, DialogTrigger } from '@/components/ui/dialog';

function MyComponent() {
  return (
    <Dialog>
      <DialogTrigger asChild>
        <Button>Open Dialog</Button>
      </DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle>Dialog Title</DialogTitle>
        </DialogHeader>
        {/* Dialog content */}
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
}
```

### Component Patterns
- Use `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Use `class-variance-authority` for component variants
- Include proper TypeScript interfaces with `React.ComponentProps` and `VariantProps`
- Add `data-slot` attributes for component identification
- Use `asChild` prop pattern for component composition

### Example Component Structure
```tsx
interface ComponentProps extends React.ComponentProps<"div"> {
  variant?: "default" | "secondary";
  size?: "sm" | "md" | "lg";
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

function Component({ className, variant = "default", size = "md", ...props }: ComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div
      data-slot="component"
      className={cn(componentVariants({ variant, size, className }))}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}
```

## Mobile-First Design Principles

### Responsive Breakpoints
- **Mobile First**: Start with mobile layout (320px-640px)
- **Breakpoints**: `sm:` (640px+), `md:` (768px+), `lg:` (1024px+), `xl:` (1280px+), `2xl:` (1536px+)
- **Pattern**: Mobile styles first, then scale up: `base-class md:desktop-class lg:large-class`

### Touch-Friendly Design
- **Minimum Tap Targets**: 44px minimum for interactive elements
- **Touch Spacing**: Adequate spacing between interactive elements
- **Gesture Support**: Consider swipe, pinch, and other mobile gestures
- **Thumb-Friendly**: Place primary actions within thumb reach

### Mobile Navigation Patterns
- **Mobile**: Use Sheet/Drawer components for navigation
- **Desktop**: Use Sidebar components for navigation
- **Pattern**: `md:hidden` for mobile-only elements, `hidden md:block` for desktop-only

## Responsive Layout Patterns

### Flexbox Patterns
```tsx
// Stack vertically on mobile, horizontal on desktop
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 md:flex-row md:gap-6">
  <div className="flex-1">Content 1</div>
  <div className="flex-1">Content 2</div>
</div>

// Mobile-first spacing
<div className="space-y-4 md:space-y-6 lg:space-y-8">
  <div>Item 1</div>
  <div>Item 2</div>
</div>
```

### Grid Layouts
```tsx
// Responsive grid: 1 column → 2 columns → 3 columns
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
  <div>Card 1</div>
  <div>Card 2</div>
  <div>Card 3</div>
</div>

// Auto-fit grid for dynamic content
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr))]">
  <div>Dynamic Card</div>
</div>
```

### Button Patterns
```tsx
// Full-width on mobile, auto-width on desktop
<Button className="w-full md:w-auto">
  Action Button
</Button>

// Responsive button sizing
<Button size="sm" className="md:size-default lg:size-lg">
  Responsive Button
</Button>
```

### Visibility Patterns
```tsx
// Show/hide based on screen size
<div className="md:hidden">Mobile Only Content</div>
<div className="hidden md:block">Desktop Only Content</div>

// Responsive text sizing
<h1 className="text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">
  Responsive Heading
</h1>
```

## Form Design Patterns

### Mobile-Optimized Forms
Follow the pattern from [resources/js/pages/auth/login.tsx](mdc:resources/js/pages/auth/login.tsx):

```tsx
<Form className="flex flex-col gap-6">
  {({ processing, errors }) => (
    <>
      <div className="grid gap-6">
        <div className="grid gap-2">
          <Label htmlFor="email">Email address</Label>
          <Input
            id="email"
            type="email"
            name="email"
            required
            autoFocus
            tabIndex={1}
            autoComplete="email"
            placeholder="email@example.com"
            className="w-full"
          />
          <InputError message={errors.email} />
        </div>
        
        <Button
          type="submit"
          className="mt-4 w-full md:w-auto"
          disabled={processing}
        >
          {processing && <LoaderCircle className="h-4 w-4 animate-spin" />}
          Submit
        </Button>
      </div>
    </>
  )}
</Form>
```

### Form Best Practices
- **Full-width inputs** on mobile: `className="w-full"`
- **Proper label associations**: Use `htmlFor` and `id` attributes
- **Error handling**: Use `InputError` component for validation messages
- **Loading states**: Show `LoaderCircle` icon during form submission
- **Accessibility**: Proper `tabIndex` management and `autoComplete` attributes
- **Inertia.js integration**: Use `Form` component for server-side validation

